The above provided output is in Debug.Assert statement. Each Debug.Assert statement ensures that the conditions are met, it's checking if Count equals to the value returned or not. The first Debug.Assert check that Count - 1 >= 0 and, the second one checks that the List.Capacity equals the original Capacity which was used while creating the list. The third Debug.Assert statement checks that the given value is present at the returned index by calling `IndexOf(value)` method which returns the first occurrence of the given element. The fourth statement checks that Count - 1 equals to the Return value (after removing the object) as specified in the question. 

The fifth statement checks the size of the list (Check if size remains same or decreases by one). The last Debug.Assert statement tests the index of the element that is actually being removed.--------------------
