Debug.Assert(IndexOf(RET) == Count - 1);
</code>

In this case, RET refers to the return value of the `Remove` method, which is the ArrayList itself. The `IndexOf` method is used to find the index of an element in the ArrayList, and the `Count` property of ArrayList gives the number of elements in the ArrayList. We are checking if the element to be removed is at the end of the list or not. And since ArrayList's remove operation decreases the size of the list, size should remain unchanged or one less. That is why we are checking for "Count - 1".--------------------